 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Notebook 03 — Instruction Dataset Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "**Assignment 1B — Enterprise Domain LLM**  \n",
    "**Author:** Abhinav Mandloi\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook:\n",
    "1. Loads the instruction dataset from `data/processed/instruction_dataset.jsonl`\n",
    "2. Displays 5 sample instruction–response pairs\n",
    "3. Analyses token statistics and plots a histogram\n",
    "4. Verifies the train/eval split\n",
    "5. Performs dataset quality analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys, json, re\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib.ticker as mticker\n",
    "\n",
    "PROJECT_ROOT   = Path('/Users/abhinavmandloi/Documents/Sem3Projects/LLM Assingment 1/enterprise-domain-llm')\n",
    "DATA_PROC_DIR  = PROJECT_ROOT / 'data' / 'processed'\n",
    "DATA_PROC_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "DATASET_PATH   = DATA_PROC_DIR / 'instruction_dataset.jsonl'\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Dataset path: {DATASET_PATH}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3.1 Generate Instruction Dataset (if not present)\n",
    "\n",
    "The instruction generator uses the cleaned domain corpus to create `(instruction, response)` pairs via heuristic templates — no external LLM is required."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "INSTRUCTION_TEMPLATES = [\n",
    "    'How do I {verb} on {os_or_platform}?',\n",
    "    'What are the steps to {verb}?',\n",
    "    'Explain how to {verb} in a production environment.',\n",
    "    'Provide a troubleshooting guide for {issue}.',\n",
    "    'What commands should I run to {verb}?',\n",
    "    'How can I diagnose and fix {issue}?',\n",
    "    'Walk me through the process of {verb}.',\n",
    "    'What is the best practice for {verb} on {os_or_platform}?',\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "VERB_ISSUE_PAIRS = [\n",
    "    ('mount an NTFS drive', 'NTFS mounting failure', 'Ubuntu'),\n",
    "    ('investigate high disk I/O', 'high disk I/O', 'Linux'),\n",
    "    ('troubleshoot SSH access issues', 'SSH connectivity failure', 'AWS EC2'),\n",
    "    ('configure a firewall with ufw', 'ufw misconfiguration', 'Ubuntu'),\n",
    "    ('monitor CPU usage', 'high CPU usage', 'Linux'),\n",
    "    ('set up an NFS share', 'NFS share unavailability', 'Linux'),\n",
    "    ('recover from a failed systemd service', 'systemd service crash', 'Linux'),\n",
    "    ('diagnose memory leaks', 'memory leak', 'Linux'),\n",
    "    ('configure swap space', 'out of memory errors', 'Linux'),\n",
    "    ('set up a VPN on EC2', 'VPN connectivity issues', 'AWS EC2'),\n",
    "    ('attach and format an EBS volume', 'EBS volume not mounting', 'AWS EC2'),\n",
    "    ('configure IAM roles for EC2', 'permission denied errors', 'AWS'),\n",
    "    ('set up CloudWatch alarms', 'missing CPU alerts', 'AWS'),\n",
    "    ('troubleshoot a failed apt upgrade', 'package dependency conflict', 'Ubuntu'),\n",
    "    ('manage cron jobs', 'cron job not running', 'Linux'),\n",
    "    ('tune kernel parameters with sysctl', 'network performance issues', 'Linux'),\n",
    "    ('configure RAID using mdadm', 'disk array failure', 'Linux'),\n",
    "    ('set up LVM logical volumes', 'disk space issues', 'Linux'),\n",
    "    ('analyse network traffic with tcpdump', 'intermittent network drops', 'Linux'),\n",
    "    ('back up and restore with rsync', 'data loss', 'Linux'),\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "RESPONSE_TEMPLATES = [\n",
    "    \"\"\"To {verb} on {platform}, follow these steps:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Verify prerequisites**: Ensure the required packages are installed (`sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y {pkg}`).\n",
    "2. **Check current status**: Run `{check_cmd}` to inspect the current state.\n",
    "3. **Apply the fix**: Execute `{fix_cmd}` to resolve the issue.\n",
    "4. **Validate the result**: Confirm with `{verify_cmd}`.\n",
    "5. **Persist the configuration**: Update `/etc/fstab` or the relevant config file for boot-time persistence.\n",
    "6. **Monitor**: Review system logs with `journalctl -xe` or `dmesg` for any residual errors.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Common pitfalls**: Ensure correct permissions (use `sudo`), verify device names (`lsblk`), and check kernel module support (`modprobe {module}`).\n",
    "\"\"\",\n",
    "    \"\"\"Troubleshooting {issue} involves a systematic approach:\n",
    "\n",
    "**Step 1 — Identify the scope**: Determine whether the problem is hardware, OS, or application-layer.\n",
    "**Step 2 — Gather diagnostics**:\n",
    "  - `{diag_cmd_1}` — real-time metrics\n",
    "  - `{diag_cmd_2}` — historical logs\n",
    "  - `{diag_cmd_3}` — process-level analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "**Step 3 — Isolate the root cause**: Compare metrics before and after the incident.\n",
    "**Step 4 — Apply remediation**: Restart the offending service, increase resource limits, or roll back a recent change.\n",
    "**Step 5 — Document and prevent**: Update runbooks and configure proactive alerting (e.g., CloudWatch, Prometheus).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reference commands**: `dmesg | tail -50`, `sar -u 1 10`, `vmstat 2 5`.\n",
    "\"\"\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "CMD_SUBSTITUTIONS = {\n",
    "    'mount an NTFS drive'                : ('ntfs-3g', 'lsblk', 'sudo mount -t ntfs-3g /dev/sdb1 /mnt/data', 'df -h /mnt/data', 'ntfs-3g', 'iostat -x 1', 'dmesg | grep -i ntfs', 'blkid'),\n",
    "    'investigate high disk I/O'          : ('sysstat', 'iostat -xz 1', 'iotop -ao', 'iostat -d 1 5', 'dm-mod', 'iotop -ao', 'journalctl -u var-log.mount', 'pidstat -d 2'),\n",
    "    'troubleshoot SSH access issues'     : ('openssh-client', 'systemctl status sshd', 'sshd -T', 'ssh -v user@host', 'ssh', 'netstat -tlnp | grep 22', 'journalctl -u sshd', 'ss -tlnp'),\n",
    "    'configure a firewall with ufw'      : ('ufw', 'ufw status verbose', 'sudo ufw allow 22/tcp', 'sudo ufw status', 'iptables', 'ufw status numbered', 'journalctl -u ufw', 'iptables -L'),\n",
    "    'monitor CPU usage'                  : ('sysstat', 'top -b -n 1', 'mpstat -P ALL 1 5', 'sar -u 1 10', 'perf', 'htop', 'vmstat 2 5', 'pidstat -u 2'),\n",
    "    'set up an NFS share'                : ('nfs-kernel-server', 'showmount -e localhost', 'sudo exportfs -a', 'mount | grep nfs', 'nfs', 'exportfs -v', 'journalctl -u nfs-server', 'rpcinfo -p'),\n",
    "    'recover from a failed systemd service': ('systemd', 'systemctl status myservice', 'sudo systemctl restart myservice', 'journalctl -u myservice -n 50', 'systemd', 'systemctl --failed', 'journalctl -xe', 'systemctl daemon-reload'),\n",
    "    'diagnose memory leaks'              : ('valgrind', 'free -h', 'valgrind --leak-check=full ./app', 'cat /proc/meminfo', 'memcheck', 'ps aux --sort=-%mem | head', 'journalctl -k | grep oom', 'smem -s rss'),\n",
    "    'configure swap space'               : ('util-linux', 'swapon --show', 'sudo fallocate -l 2G /swapfile && sudo mkswap /swapfile && sudo swapon /swapfile', 'free -h', 'swap', 'cat /proc/swaps', 'dmesg | grep -i swap', 'vmstat -s'),\n",
    "    'set up a VPN on EC2'               : ('openvpn', 'systemctl status openvpn', 'sudo openvpn --config /etc/openvpn/server.conf', 'ip route show', 'tun', 'netstat -tlnp | grep 1194', 'journalctl -u openvpn', 'ip addr show tun0'),\n",
    "    'attach and format an EBS volume'   : ('util-linux', 'lsblk', 'sudo mkfs.ext4 /dev/xvdf && sudo mount /dev/xvdf /data', 'df -h /data', 'ext4', 'aws ec2 describe-volumes', 'dmesg | tail -20', 'blkid'),\n",
    "    'configure IAM roles for EC2'       : ('awscli', 'aws iam list-roles', 'aws ec2 associate-iam-instance-profile', 'curl http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/iam/', 'iam', 'aws sts get-caller-identity', 'cloud-init-output.log', 'aws ec2 describe-iam-instance-profile-associations'),\n",
    "    'set up CloudWatch alarms'          : ('awscli', 'aws cloudwatch list-metrics', 'aws cloudwatch put-metric-alarm', 'aws cloudwatch describe-alarms', 'cloudwatch', 'aws cloudwatch get-metric-statistics', 'CloudTrail', 'aws cloudwatch list-dashboards'),\n",
    "    'troubleshoot a failed apt upgrade' : ('apt', 'apt list --installed', 'sudo apt-get -f install && sudo apt-get autoremove', 'apt-cache policy pkg', 'dpkg', 'dpkg --audit', 'journalctl -u apt-daily.service', 'apt-get check'),\n",
    "    'manage cron jobs'                  : ('cron', 'crontab -l', 'crontab -e', 'systemctl status cron', 'cron', 'grep CRON /var/log/syslog', 'journalctl -u cron', 'run-parts --test /etc/cron.daily'),\n",
    "    'tune kernel parameters with sysctl': ('procps', 'sysctl -a | grep net', 'sudo sysctl -w net.core.somaxconn=1024', 'sysctl net.core.somaxconn', 'kernel', 'cat /proc/sys/net/core/somaxconn', 'dmesg | grep -i network', 'ip link show'),\n",
    "    'configure RAID using mdadm'        : ('mdadm', 'cat /proc/mdstat', 'sudo mdadm --create /dev/md0 --level=1 --raid-devices=2 /dev/sdb /dev/sdc', 'mdadm --detail /dev/md0', 'md', 'mdadm --examine /dev/sdb', 'journalctl -k | grep md', 'cat /etc/mdadm/mdadm.conf'),\n",
    "    'set up LVM logical volumes'        : ('lvm2', 'pvs && vgs && lvs', 'sudo pvcreate /dev/sdb && sudo vgcreate vg0 /dev/sdb && sudo lvcreate -L 10G -n lv0 vg0', 'df -h /dev/vg0/lv0', 'dm-mod', 'lvdisplay', 'journalctl -k | grep lvm', 'vgdisplay'),\n",
    "    'analyse network traffic with tcpdump': ('tcpdump', 'ip link show', 'sudo tcpdump -i eth0 -n -w /tmp/capture.pcap', 'tcpdump -r /tmp/capture.pcap | head -20', 'pcap', 'netstat -s', 'journalctl -k | grep -i eth0', 'ss -s'),\n",
    "    'back up and restore with rsync'    : ('rsync', 'df -h /backup', 'rsync -avz --progress /source/ user@remote:/backup/', 'rsync --dry-run -avz /source/ /backup/', 'fuse', 'du -sh /backup/*', 'tail -f /var/log/rsync.log', 'diff -r /source/ /backup/'),\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "records = []\n",
    "import random\n",
    "random.seed(42)\n",
    "\n",
    "for verb, issue, platform in VERB_ISSUE_PAIRS:\n",
    "    subs = CMD_SUBSTITUTIONS.get(verb, ('pkg', 'check_cmd', 'fix_cmd', 'verify_cmd', 'module', 'diag1', 'diag2', 'diag3'))\n",
    "    for _ in range(10):  # 10 pairs per topic = 200 total\n",
    "        tmpl = random.choice(INSTRUCTION_TEMPLATES)\n",
    "        resp_tmpl = random.choice(RESPONSE_TEMPLATES)\n",
    "        instruction = tmpl.format(verb=verb, os_or_platform=platform, issue=issue)\n",
    "        response = resp_tmpl.format(\n",
    "            verb=verb, platform=platform, issue=issue,\n",
    "            pkg=subs[0], check_cmd=subs[1], fix_cmd=subs[2],\n",
    "            verify_cmd=subs[3], module=subs[4],\n",
    "            diag_cmd_1=subs[5], diag_cmd_2=subs[6], diag_cmd_3=subs[7]\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        records.append({'instruction': instruction.strip(), 'response': response.strip()})\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Generated {len(records):,} instruction-response pairs.')\n",
    "\n",
    "if not DATASET_PATH.exists():\n",
    "    with open(DATASET_PATH, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n",
    "        for rec in records:\n",
    "            f.write(json.dumps(rec) + '\\n')\n",
    "    print(f'Saved to {DATASET_PATH}')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f'Dataset already exists at {DATASET_PATH}, loading it.')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load\n",
    "dataset = []\n",
    "with open(DATASET_PATH, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n",
    "    for line in f:\n",
    "        dataset.append(json.loads(line.strip()))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Loaded {len(dataset):,} records.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3.2 Sample Inspection: 5 Instruction–Response Pairs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "for i, rec in enumerate(dataset[:5]):\n",
    "    print(f'\\n--- Sample {i+1} ---')\n",
    "    print(f'INSTRUCTION: {rec[\"instruction\"]}')\n",
    "    print(f'RESPONSE    :\\n{rec[\"response\"][:300]}...')\n",
    "    print()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3.3 Token Statistics"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from transformers import AutoTokenizer\n",
    "\n",
    "tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained('Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct', trust_remote_code=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Computing token counts...')\n",
    "instr_lens = [len(tokenizer.encode(r['instruction'])) for r in dataset]\n",
    "resp_lens  = [len(tokenizer.encode(r['response']))    for r in dataset]\n",
    "total_lens = [i + r for i, r in zip(instr_lens, resp_lens)]\n",
    "\n",
    "token_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'Metric'           : ['Instruction tokens', 'Response tokens', 'Total tokens'],\n",
    "    'Mean'             : [np.mean(instr_lens), np.mean(resp_lens), np.mean(total_lens)],\n",
    "    'Median'           : [np.median(instr_lens), np.median(resp_lens), np.median(total_lens)],\n",
    "    'Min'              : [np.min(instr_lens), np.min(resp_lens), np.min(total_lens)],\n",
    "    'Max'              : [np.max(instr_lens), np.max(resp_lens), np.max(total_lens)],\n",
    "    'P95'              : [np.percentile(instr_lens, 95), np.percentile(resp_lens, 95), np.percentile(total_lens, 95)],\n",
    "})\n",
    "token_df[['Mean','Median','Min','Max','P95']] = token_df[['Mean','Median','Min','Max','P95']].applymap(lambda x: round(x, 1))\n",
    "print(token_df.to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3.4 Token Length Histogram"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(15, 4))\n",
    "titles = ['Instruction Token Lengths', 'Response Token Lengths', 'Total Token Lengths']\n",
    "data   = [instr_lens, resp_lens, total_lens]\n",
    "colours = ['#4C72B0', '#55A868', '#C44E52']\n",
    "\n",
    "for ax, d, title, colour in zip(axes, data, titles, colours):\n",
    "    ax.hist(d, bins=25, color=colour, edgecolor='white', alpha=0.85)\n",
    "    ax.axvline(np.mean(d), color='black', linestyle='--', linewidth=1.5, label=f'Mean {np.mean(d):.0f}')\n",
    "    ax.set_title(title, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel('Token Count')\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel('Frequency')\n",
    "    ax.legend(fontsize=8)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "charts_dir = PROJECT_ROOT / 'results' / 'charts'\n",
    "charts_dir.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "plt.savefig(charts_dir / 'token_distribution.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "print('Chart saved.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3.5 Train / Eval Split"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import random\n",
    "\n",
    "random.seed(42)\n",
    "shuffled = dataset.copy()\n",
    "random.shuffle(shuffled)\n",
    "\n",
    "TRAIN_RATIO = 0.9\n",
    "split_idx   = int(len(shuffled) * TRAIN_RATIO)\n",
    "train_set   = shuffled[:split_idx]\n",
    "eval_set    = shuffled[split_idx:]\n",
    "\n",
    "train_path = DATA_PROC_DIR / 'train_dataset.jsonl'\n",
    "eval_path  = DATA_PROC_DIR / 'eval_dataset.jsonl'\n",
    "\n",
    "with open(train_path, 'w') as f:\n",
    "    for r in train_set:\n",
    "        f.write(json.dumps(r) + '\\n')\n",
    "\n",
    "with open(eval_path, 'w') as f:\n",
    "    for r in eval_set:\n",
    "        f.write(json.dumps(r) + '\\n')\n",
    "\n",
    "split_df = pd.DataFrame([\n",
    "    {'Split': 'Train', 'Records': len(train_set), 'Fraction': f'{len(train_set)/len(shuffled)*100:.1f}%'},\n",
    "    {'Split': 'Eval',  'Records': len(eval_set),  'Fraction': f'{len(eval_set)/len(shuffled)*100:.1f}%'},\n",
    "    {'Split': 'Total', 'Records': len(shuffled),  'Fraction': '100.0%'},\n",
    "])\n",
    "print('Train/Eval Split:')\n",
    "print(split_df.to_string(index=False))\n",
    "print(f'\\nSaved: {train_path}')\n",
    "print(f'Saved: {eval_path}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3.6 Dataset Quality Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "| Quality Check | Result |\n",
    "|--------------|--------|\n",
    "| All records have `instruction` field | ✅ |\n",
    "| All records have `response` field | ✅ |\n",
    "| No empty instructions | ✅ |\n",
    "| No empty responses | ✅ |\n",
    "| Avg total tokens < model context limit (128K) | ✅ |\n",
    "| Domain coverage (IT topics) | ✅ 20 topics |\n",
    "| Template diversity | ✅ 8 instruction templates, 2 response templates |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Automated quality checks\n",
    "checks = {\n",
    "    'All have instruction': all('instruction' in r for r in dataset),\n",
    "    'All have response'   : all('response'    in r for r in dataset),\n",
    "    'No empty instruction': all(len(r['instruction'].strip()) > 0 for r in dataset),\n",
    "    'No empty response'   : all(len(r['response'].strip()) > 0 for r in dataset),\n",
    "    'Max total tokens < 1024': max(total_lens) < 1024,\n",
    "    'Dataset size >= 100' : len(dataset) >= 100,\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "for check, result in checks.items():\n",
    "    icon = '✅' if result else '❌'\n",
    "    print(f'  {icon} {check}: {result}')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('\\nDataset quality checks passed.' if all(checks.values()) else '\\n⚠ Some checks failed — review above.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata":",
   "source": [
